367:  of `/resolve` calls (any non-power contest) never touch `chapters`/`game_sessions`/`territories`
368:  at all — no new DB load added to the common path.
369:- **`defender_pool: null` is now reachable for TWO distinct reasons**, both meaning "not finalised
370:  yet": no `defender_aspect` (crd-3b, unchanged) and — new here — the gate open with no
371:  `defender_status_term` submitted. The clamp step (`Math.max(0, Math.min(30, ...))`) is
372:  deliberately skipped when the pool is `null`, since `Math.min(30, null)` silently coerces to `0`
373:  (a real, wrong total) rather than staying `null` — caught while writing the code, not by a test
374:  failure.
375:- **`status_choice` is attached to the response object AFTER the Mongo re-fetch**, not persisted —
376:  it is a live-computed value only meaningful for the response that produced it (the values would
377:  go stale the moment either character's City Status changes). `defender_status_term` (which term
378:  was picked) is the only piece of this mechanic that persists on the document.
379:- **Client discard-on-close (AC9)** happens inside `_resolve`'s own success branch: any response
380:  without an eligible `status_choice` clears both `state.statusChoice` and `state.statusTerm`
381:  together, so a stale selection can never silently ride along into a re-opened gate under
382:  different numbers on a later call.
